{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "All's Well That Ends Well"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Together Like Always"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe emotions and feelings in present and past situations in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spit it out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to urge someone to say or confess something quickly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Ok. Peter spit it out."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when someone is angry."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "what's eating you?"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "what is annoying or bothering you?"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What's eating you? Is it the trip?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le16ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Comparative Clause: Degree"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Comparisons express differences or similarities based on a judgement or standard of measurement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use comparative clauses, your English sounds more dynamic and mature.   </br></br>You introduce adverbial clauses of comparison of degree with the subordinating conjunction <span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"italic\">than</span></span>, or by the relative adverb <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">as</span><span class=\"italic\">."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: </br></br><span class=\"italic\">  I am older <span class=\"strong\">than my brother</span>. </br>He doesn't work harder <span class=\"strong\">than we do</span>.</br> My mother earns more <span class=\"strong\">than my father</span>.</br> He is as smart <span class=\"strong\">as he is handsome</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sometimes I feel I am more serious about this relationship <span class=\"strong\">than</span> you are."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You are more upset <span class=\"strong\">than</span> I expected about this."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Candace is as secretive <span class=\"strong\">as</span> she is intelligent."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This may not be less lucrative <span class=\"strong\">than</span> my other job, but rest assured it is much more rewarding and important."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">Comparative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"as ... as\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The same\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They are <span class=\\\"strong\\\">as tall as</span> each other.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"-er than\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"More\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He is <span class=\\\"strong\\\">better than</span> his brother at soccer.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more than\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Much\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Kelly has done <span class=\\\"strong\\\">more than</span> her share of the cleaning.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"less than\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Fewer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Susan has done <span class=\\\"strong\\\">less than</span> the others in the group.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"further than\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Farther\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The team had been pushed <span class=\\\"strong\\\">further than</span> the other teams combined.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the more ... the more\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Increasing at the same time/rate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">The more</span> things change <span class=\\\"strong\\\">the more</span> things stay the same.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals to Express Annoyance in the Past "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to express annoyance and criticism about the past, you can use modals. Modals such as <span class=\"strong\">could</span>, <span class=\"strong\">might</span>, <span class=\"strong\">should</span>, <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">would not</span> add meaning to the main verb and can convey annoyance when you use them properly."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about annoyance in the past, you use the modal + have + past participle. </br>Let's look at some modals and their meanings:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. <span class=\"strong\">Could have / Might have</span> - to make a critical comment  </br></br><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">could have had</span> an accident. </br>We <span class=\"strong\">might have all been </span>infected.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "2. <span class=\"strong\">Could have / Might have</span> - to express annoyance   </br></br><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">might have told </span>me before it happened. </br>She <span class=\"strong\">could have RSVP'd</span>, at least."}, {"type": "text", "content": "3. <span class=\"strong\">Should have / Ought to have</span> - to express annoyance or criticism  </br></br><span class=\"italic\">You<span class=\"strong\"> should have taken</span> his advice. </br>They <span class=\"strong\">ought to have done </span>something about it by now! </br>You <span class=\"strong\">should have handed</span> in your assignment on time.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "4. <span class=\"strong\">Would not have</span> - to express annoyance </br></br> It <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't have hurt</span> her to visit him now and then.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You <span class=\"strong\">might have</span> given me a heads up before lunch today. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Candace and I <span class=\"strong\">may have</span> had some correspondence about it back and forth."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You <span class=\"strong\">could have</span> informed me a little earlier."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">may have</span> known about your volunteering, but I just wish I could have been a part of your decision to go to Africa. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "heads up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "advance notice"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You might have given me a heads up before lunch today. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lucrative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "producing a great deal of profit"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This may be less lucrative than my other job."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rest assured"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to be \u200bcertain that something will \u200bhappen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Rest assured it is much more rewarding."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rewarding"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "providing satisfaction; gratifying"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is much more rewarding and important."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research four idioms about anger and annoyance."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a powerpoint presentation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain my idioms clearly and concisely."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use my idioms in sentences or conversations to help better explain."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a unique way to test my classmates knowledge."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, research four idioms or expressions about anger or annoyance."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a powerpoint presentation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Your presentation should include the idiom and the meaning as well as images to help people understand the idiom better."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the idioms in a sentence or in a conversation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your powerpoint to the class."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The presentation should be about 5 minutes in length."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a unique way to test your classmates after about the idioms they just heard."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about beliefs, opinions, relationships or character traits."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express comparison between two things or events."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express annoyance about an action or an event in the past."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you do when you are angry at someone?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think people should do when they get angry?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What do you do to avoid getting angry?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2